@page "/"

<PageTitle>Blazor Circuit Telemetry</PageTitle>
<svg width="0" height="0" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <defs>
        <clipPath id="telemetry-tab-shape" clipPathUnits="objectBoundingBox">
            <path d="M .12 0 H .72 C .82 0 .80 .42 .86 .68 C .90 .88 .95 1 1 1 H 0 V .1 A .15 .15 0 0 1 .15 0 Z" />
        </clipPath>
    </defs>
</svg>
<div class="internals-page">
    <header><p class="eyebrow">Development-only diagnostic POC</p><h1>Interactive Server circuit telemetry</h1><p>This static SSR host contains two sibling islands: the playground runs on Interactive Server; the terminal runs locally in Interactive WebAssembly and observes it without adding traffic to its circuit.</p></header>
    <div class="islands">
        <BlazorServerPlayground @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
        <BlazorTelemetryTerminal @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
    </div>

    <section id="protocol-reference" class="protocol-reference" aria-labelledby="protocol-reference-title">
        <details>
            <summary>
                <span><span class="eyebrow">Built-in documentation</span><strong id="protocol-reference-title">How the telemetry is decoded</strong></span>
                <span class="summary-hint">Protocol reference</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="reference-content">
                <p class="reference-intro">The decoder combines the documented SignalR MessagePack protocol with Blazor's internal circuit method contracts. Blazor circuit messages are implementation details and may change between .NET releases.</p>

                <div class="reference-grid">
                    <article>
                        <h2>Binary envelope</h2>
                        <pre><code>[VarInt length][MessagePack body]</code></pre>
                        <dl class="byte-example">
                            <div><dt><code>02</code></dt><dd>Body length: 2 bytes</dd></div>
                            <div><dt><code>91</code></dt><dd>MessagePack array with one item</dd></div>
                            <div><dt><code>06</code></dt><dd>SignalR message type 6: Ping</dd></div>
                        </dl>
                    </article>

                    <article>
                        <h2>Invocation envelope</h2>
                        <pre><code>[1, Headers, InvocationId, Target, Arguments, StreamIds]</code></pre>
                        <p>Targets such as <code>JS.RenderBatch</code>, <code>OnRenderCompleted</code>, and <code>JS.EndInvokeDotNet</code> identify Blazor circuit operations inside ordinary SignalR invocations.</p>
                    </article>

                    <article>
                        <h2>Render lifecycle</h2>
                        <ol class="render-flow">
                            <li><code>JS.RenderBatch</code><span>Server sends a render-tree diff and batch ID.</span></li>
                            <li><code>OnRenderCompleted</code><span>Browser reports whether that batch was applied.</span></li>
                            <li><code>JS.EndInvokeDotNet</code><span>A JavaScript-initiated .NET call returns its result.</span></li>
                        </ol>
                    </article>

                    <article>
                        <h2>Terminal classification</h2>
                        <ul class="classification-list">
                            <li><strong>RawFrame</strong><span>Original WebSocket payload as copyable hex.</span></li>
                            <li><strong>SignalR</strong><span>Ping, Invocation, Completion, Close, Ack, and Sequence.</span></li>
                            <li><strong>Circuit</strong><span>Decoded Blazor targets and correlated render batches.</span></li>
                            <li><strong>Annotation</strong><span>Events deliberately emitted by this POC.</span></li>
                        </ul>
                    </article>
                </div>

                <div class="official-sources">
                    <h2>Official Microsoft sources</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><a href="https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/v10.0.10/src/SignalR/docs/specs/HubProtocol.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SignalR Hub Protocol specification</a><span>Message types, MessagePack layouts, Ping bytes, and VarInt framing.</span></li>
                        <li><a href="https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/v10.0.10/src/SignalR/common/Protocols.MessagePack/src/Protocol/MessagePackHubProtocol.cs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SignalR MessagePack implementation</a><span>The production parser and writer.</span></li>
                        <li><a href="https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/v10.0.10/src/Components/Web.JS/src/Platform/Circuits/CircuitManager.ts" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Blazor browser circuit manager</a><span>Handlers for RenderBatch and .NET interop completion.</span></li>
                        <li><a href="https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/v10.0.10/src/Components/Server/src/Circuits/RemoteRenderer.cs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Blazor server remote renderer</a><span>Sends render batches and tracks acknowledgements.</span></li>
                        <li><a href="https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/v10.0.10/src/Components/Server/src/ComponentHub.cs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Blazor ComponentHub</a><span>Receives browser circuit calls such as OnRenderCompleted.</span></li>
                        <li><a href="https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/v10.0.10/src/Components/Web.JS/src/Rendering/RenderBatch/OutOfProcessRenderBatch.ts" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RenderBatch binary reader</a><span>Reads the internal render-tree diff payload in the browser.</span></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </details>
    </section>
</div>
